  "description": "Where a landing's time goes, one point per land.sh run. land.sh writes a logfmt line to syslog from its EXIT trap (`logger -t landing-annotation`), promtail ships it to Loki, and this board reads it. wait_merge is `--await-merge` polling until the PR merged; wait_ci is master CI on the merge commit, plus any wait on a newer tip when another PR merged mid-landing; tick is the GitOps tick; deploy is the scoped deploy.sh run. Empty phases were never reached (a `blocked` landing has no wait_ci). `cause` names which deploy failure a `deploy-failed` verdict was, and is empty beside every other verdict. Every panel drops the test fixtures the `land.sh` suite wrote to the real syslog until 2026-09-03 (`_no_syslog` in scripts/deploy_tools/tests/conftest.py closed the leak). They are 8,282 of the 8,777 records Loki holds, and the discriminator is the PR id alone: `pr` 939, 999 and 999999 are the numbers the fixtures pass, and `pr=unknown` is an argparse failure, which carries no sha and no phase timing whatever wrote it. The regex is anchored because `pr !~ \"999\"` unanchored also eats `pr=999999` and would eat a real PR 1999 later. Do NOT add `sha!=\"\"`: a real landing that aborts before the merge has an empty sha too, and filtering on it removes most genuine `aborted` rows. CLI equivalent: `uv run python scripts/diagnostics/probe.py loki-query '{job=\"syslog\"} |= \"event=landing\" | logfmt | pr !~ \"^(939|999|999999|unknown)$\"'`.",
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "id": null,
